  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 955 PM MDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nAs outflow boundaries continue to slosh about the lowlands this \nevening, isolated to scattered showers/storms may develop. Some \nactivity may produce gusty winds to 30 mph with brief downpours \nbefore the convection fizzles out by around midnight. Moisture level \nlook to increase slightly for the weekend (PWs around 1.25\" at KELP) \nwith storm chances favoring area mountains. WPC has issued a Slight \nERO for Saturday across the northern tier of the CWA with the HREF \nshowing 1-2\" 24-hr max rainfall totals in the Sacs and Gila. \nIsolated instances of flash flooding can be seen in area mtns and \nout west tomorrow PM with storm motion to the southwest. Rain \nchances will be lower as you head south and east with gusty outflows \nand some blowing dust being the main threats. Sunday looks similar \nwith generally isolated to scattered coverage and best chances of \nheavy rainfall out west. \n\nTo begin the new workweek, drier air filters in from the east, \nlowering storm chances into midweek. The mtns will keep a low chance \nof storms each afternoon, more so the Gila where moisture is a bit \nhigher, with gusty outflows possible for the lowlands. Mainly dry \nconditions are forecast after Sunday for the lowlands. The heat will \nbe the primary hazard through next week as the monsoonal high sits \njust to our north over the Southern Rockies/Four Corners region. \nLowland high temperatures remain in the 100-105F range most days \nwith possible Heat Advisories for the lower RGV, like we saw today. \nThere's medium to high confidence in this extended stretch of hot \ntemps.",
